While there may be practical benefits to communities having shared cultural or social backgrounds—such as stronger bonds and mutual understanding—it is ultimately more beneficial for society as a whole to foster integration and mutual respect across differences. History has shown that when people are allowed to interact freely and learn from one another, we become more tolerant, innovative, and capable of solving complex problems that affect everyone.

