Publicly funded broadcasting can act as a check on commercial interests and provide access to information and viewpoints that might not otherwise be represented. It also ensures that media remains accessible to all citizens, regardless of socioeconomic status. However, it is crucial that oversight mechanisms are in place to prevent any institution, regardless of its content independence, from becoming politically or financially influenced in ways that compromise objectivity.

