I think the real question is not whether the rich are taxed enough, but whether the system is fair and effective without discouraging economic dynamism. In Denmark, we value a fair society and collective responsibility, but we also recognize the importance of rewarding innovation and risk-taking. Perhaps the challenge lies in finding a balance: high enough to redistribute and fund public needs, but not so high that it undermines the drive to succeed and create wealth.

In conclusion, while the rich are indeed taxed quite heavily in Denmark, the debate should focus on refining the rates to ensure they remain both just and productive for society as a whole." }

