From a Danish perspective, our military has a long tradition of upholding international law and contributing to multilateral security arrangements like NATO. This commitment is rooted in our values of responsibility and solidarity with other nations. Therefore, while I do not agree that defying international law is ever truly justified, I acknowledge the complexity of global challenges. Still, any deviation from the law should be a last resort, accompanied by a clear demonstration of necessity and a commitment to restoring international order as quickly as possible. Ultimately, the rule of law must be preserved, even in difficult times, to safeguard humanity as a whole." }

