While it is important to ensure that no one is denied essential healthcare due to financial constraints, I believe that allowing those who can afford it to opt for higher standards of care aligns with principles of fairness and personal responsibility. It also encourages innovation and quality improvement within the healthcare sector, as providers can invest more in advanced treatments for patients who are willing to pay. 

