To the question of whether abortion should always be illegal when a woman's life is not threatened, I would say that it is not fair or just to impose the same rule for everyone, regardless of their background or circumstances. Life circumstances can vary greatly, and what is considered 'threatening' to a woman's life can be subjective. Moreover, laws that are too rigid can cause harm, especially to women who face unsafe or illegal options due to restrictive policies.

