Today, more and more mothers in South Korea—and around the world—are pursuing successful careers while also being dedicated mothers. Many women balance both roles effectively, recognizing that being a good mother does not mean sacrificing their own ambitions, personal growth, or contributions to society. A career allows mothers to provide for their families, make independent decisions, and model resilience and empowerment to their children.

