Charity, on the other hand, often relies on voluntary donations and can be limited by the capacity of donors and the transparency of how funds are used. It can also be vulnerable to corruption or misallocation. Social security, by contrast, is funded by contributions from working citizens and is intended to be accountable and fairer for all.

