However, history and modern experience show that societies thrive not by rigidly segregating people based on innate characteristics, but by encouraging voluntary associations, mutual respect, and the protection of individual freedoms within the bounds of law and shared civic values. Diversity, when embraced responsibly, can lead to innovation, cultural enrichment, and a more resilient society capable of adapting to change. 

