While it is true that cultural and systemic barriers may exist, history and contemporary examples abound of immigrants who have not only adapted but thrived. Full integration, in its essence, means achieving equal access to opportunities and respect within the community. This requires effort from both immigrants and host societies—through language learning, civic engagement, and mutual understanding. 

Rather than accepting a blanket statement of impossibility, it is more constructive to focus on how both immigrants and host communities can work together to overcome obstacles and foster genuine inclusion. The strength of a nation lies in its ability to embrace diversity and support all citizens in reaching their potential." }

