While businesses should be held to high standards of honesty and transparency, I would argue that penalizing them for honest mistakes or legitimate, if perhaps poorly communicated, business strategies could be counterproductive. The focus should be on ensuring that any penalties are fair, proportionate, and based on clear evidence of intentional deception or fraud—actions that can harm consumers and undermine trust in markets.

